  "title": "StockStatementScreen uses 'as any' type assertions to call stock status helpers",
  "description": "R6 deep audit finding. Dimension: security. Severity: P3. Source SHA: bbd487a3. Scope: R6_DEEP_AUDIT_WAVE. The StockCard component casts item.stockStatus (typed as string) to any before passing it to getStockStatusColor() and getStockStatusLabel(). This bypasses TypeScript's type safety and could lead to runtime errors if the API returns unexpected stock status values that the helper functions don't handle.",
